# The benchd measurement binary and its manifest, resolved by
# tools/fetch-benchd.sh from the bench repository's dist channel. A FETCHED
# ARTIFACT, never repository content: the channel publishes
# benchd.manifest.json beside the binary, the bytes are verified against that
# manifest on every resolve, and the resolved pair is installed here. Committing
# them would add a 2 MB blob to the history that carries no authority the
# channel manifest does not already carry.
/benchd-bin/

# Build artifacts
*.so
build/
dist/
.build/
# Cargo's build tree, at any depth. The protocol adapter under harness/ is a
# cargo crate, and its `target/` is a build artifact the way `.build/` is for
# SwiftPM -- never repository content. Unanchored on purpose, so a second
# crate cannot reintroduce the same 150 MB of object files, registry paths and
# host toolchain records by living somewhere this rule did not name.
target/
.build-worker/
.build-ci/
.tools/
.mlxfast-cache/
.mlxfast-private/
.cache/

# Reference weights are large and downloaded by setup.sh
reference_weights/*
!reference_weights/.gitkeep

# Participant transformed weights are gitignored by default; opt in if needed.
# The seed's offline transform (Sources/MLXFastTransform) that produced weights/
# was removed with the Swift package in the final de-Swift; this ignore is kept
# so a hand-staged experiment cannot be committed by a stray `git add -A`, and
# so a returning weights/ directory is ignored rather than swept into a
# submission diff. NO .gitkeep here (unlike reference_weights/ above): weights/
# is not a benchmark.json editablePaths entry, so it need not pre-exist.
weights/*

# The speculative head directory. This track's MTP head is a SEPARATE pinned
# Q8_0 GGUF that the organizer stages in the target snapshot beside the shards,
# so nothing stages a head weight file here and no submission carries one.
# mtp-head/ IS a benchmark.json editablePaths entry, and so is its DECLARATION,
# mtp-head.manifest.json. The directory's README.md is tracked already. The
# ignore stays so a hand-staged weight experiment cannot be committed into the
# tree by a stray `git add -A`.
mtp-head/

# Local results log
results.tsv
m5_artifacts/

# Benchmark contract outputs
score.json
score.json.tmp
# Every local run also writes a checksum sidecar and an integrity record, and
# --local-iterate writes its own score/integrity names (benchmark.sh:112,:190).
# Leaving them untracked-but-not-ignored made the tree permanently dirty, so a
# `git add -A` swept repo-root artifacts into a submission diff -- which
# enforce-modifiable-surface.sh then rejects as outside editablePaths.
score.json.sha256
score.local-*.json
score.local-*.json.sha256
score*.baseline.json
benchmark-integrity.json
benchmark-integrity.local-*.json
correctness_golden.json
correctness_golden*.json
local_correctness_golden.json
private_prompts.json
private_prompts*.json
gpqa_reference_cases.json
gpqa_reference_cases*.json
correctness_prompts/*correctness_golden*.json
correctness_prompts/*golden_prompt*.json
correctness_prompts/*golden_prompt*.txt
correctness_prompts/*private*.json
correctness_prompts/*private*.txt
correctness_prompts/*gpqa_reference_cases*.json

# IDE
.vscode/
.idea/
.serena/
*.swp
*.swo
.DS_Store

# Local-only working docs (not part of the benchmark)
local-docs/
__pycache__/

# Operator-local environment: endpoints and credentials belong here, never in the repo
.env

